8) Training recipe (concise actionable)
	•	Stage 0 (optional): Pretrain Q‑former on generic image→text (image captions + VQA) for 1–2 epochs. BLIP‑2 uses 2-stage.  ￼
	•	Stage 1: Finetune Q‑former + LoRA adapters on your UI dataset (image → serialized JSON). Freeze vision & LLM initial layers if memory limited.
	•	Losses: L_total = L_CE(tokens) + λ_box * L1(boxes) if you include box head. Set λ_box ~ 1.0.
	•	Optim: AdamW, lr 1e‑4 (LoRA & Q‑former), batch size 32 effective (accumulation), mixed precision.
	•	Eval: structural F1 (IoU > 0.5 + class match), coordinate MAE, attribute accuracies.

⸻

9) Deployment advice
	•	Best accuracy: keep LLM on server, run inference via an API (mobile sends screenshot).
	•	Edge/On‑device: export ViT‑G to ONNX/TensorRT for faster feature extraction; run smaller LLM or quantized LLM on edge (big accuracy drop).
	•	Latency tricks: cache vision encoder outputs for identical UIs; use smaller K (32) for faster decoding.

