Prompt:

You are given a screenshot of the dropdown Quick Settings panel from a Samsung smartphone.
Identify all visible toggle elements such as:
	•	Airplane Mode
	•	Bluetooth
	•	Wi-Fi
	•	Mobile Data
	•	Location
	•	Do Not Disturb
	•	Hotspot
	•	Torch/Flashlight
	•	Power Saving Mode
	•	Any other visible quick setting icons

For each detected element, return its name and current state (On or Off).

Rules:
	•	The name must exactly match the icon’s function (e.g., “Bluetooth” instead of “BT”).
	•	The state should be On if the icon appears active (highlighted or colored) and Off if inactive (greyed out).
	•	If an element is partially visible but recognizable, still include it.
	•	Do not include elements that are not part of the quick settings panel.

Output format (JSON):

[
  {"name": "Wi-Fi", "state": "On"},
  {"name": "Bluetooth", "state": "Off"},
  {"name": "Airplane Mode", "state": "Off"}
]



